propertyDetail.informationFor                    = Information for:
propertyDetail.publicInformation                 = Public information
propertyDetail.publicInformation.anybody         = Anybody can view this information
propertyDetail.band                              = Council Tax band
propertyDetail.band.hint                         = The current band for the property. This is based on the property value on 01 April 1991.
propertyDetail.band.expand                       = Council Tax bands England
propertyDetail.band.table.band                   = Band
propertyDetail.band.table.value                  = Property value at 1 April 1991
propertyDetail.band.current                      = current band
propertyDetail.band.range.A                      = up to £40,000
propertyDetail.band.range.B                      = £40,001 to £52,000
propertyDetail.band.range.C                      = £52,001 to £68,000
propertyDetail.band.range.D                      = £68,001 to £88,000
propertyDetail.band.range.E                      = £88,001 to £120,000
propertyDetail.band.range.F                      = £120,001 to £160,000
propertyDetail.band.range.G                      = £160,001 to £320,000
propertyDetail.band.range.H                      = More than £320,000
propertyDetail.effectiveFrom                     = With effect from
propertyDetail.effectiveFrom.hint                = The date the current band came into effect.
propertyDetail.localCouncil                      = Local Council
propertyDetail.localCouncil.hint                 = The Local Council sets the amount of Council Tax you pay each year, based on the band.
propertyDetail.councilRef                        = Local Council reference number
propertyDetail.councilRef.hint                   = A reference number for the property.
propertyDetail.improvement                       = Improvement indicator
propertyDetail.improvement.hint                  = If a property has been improved or extended since it was placed in a Council Tax band, a Yes will be shown. This means the band will be reviewed and may increase following the sale of the property.
propertyDetail.mixedUse                          = Mixed-use property
propertyDetail.mixedUse.hint                     = A property which is used as a home and a business. For example, a working farm or a flat above a shop.
propertyDetail.courtCode                         = Court code
propertyDetail.courtCode.hint                    = If the Council Tax band has been reviewed by a Valuation Tribunal or High Court, a court code will be shown.
propertyDetail.courtCode.none                    = None
propertyDetail.courtCode.expand                  = What the codes mean
propertyDetail.courtCode.meaning                 = Court codes indicate the outcome of a tribunal or court review of the Council Tax band.
propertyDetail.courtCode.V                       = Valuation Tribunal determination
propertyDetail.courtCode.C                       = Valuation Tribunal confirmation
propertyDetail.courtCode.R                       = Valuation Tribunal redetermination following High Court referral
propertyDetail.courtCode.D                       = High Court determination
propertyDetail.courtCode.H                       = High Court confirmation
propertyDetail.courtCode.E                       = High Court consent order
propertyDetail.beforeYouContinue                 = Before you continue
propertyDetail.beforeYouContinue.youCan          = You can:
propertyDetail.beforeYouContinue.viewPrevious    = View previous Council Tax bands for this property
propertyDetail.beforeYouContinue.challenge       = tell us if you think the Council Tax band is wrong if you pay Council Tax for the property, or have permission from the Council Tax payer
propertyDetail.beforeYouContinue.remove          = ask us to remove the property from the Council Tax list if it has been demolished, is derelict, or is undergoing major renovation.
propertyDetail.beforeYouContinue.signIn          = You''ll need a GOV Gateway or GOV.UK One Login Account to sign in.

 
